    "# Part 1A — Causal Counterfactual + Activation-Patching Interventions\n",
    "## Scratch Transformer / Markov state experiment\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook adds one targeted experiment to the existing **Part 1 — Markov Context Sufficiency** pipeline without modifying any previous run or checkpoint.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Questions\n",
    "1. Once the full order-\\(k\\) Markov state is observable (\\(L\\ge k\\)), does the **native output head** track a counterfactual change to the state-defining input?\n",
    "2. Does an **internal residual-stream activation** induced by that state change causally steer the native prediction toward the corresponding counterfactual oracle?\n",
    "\n",
    "### Design\n",
    "For each \\(k\\in\\{2,3,4\\}\\), seed \\(0,\\dots,4\\), and \\(L\\in\\{k,k+1\\}\\), the input-intervention stage loads the existing trained checkpoint and exact saved transition kernel, samples held-out stationary contexts, changes the oldest token inside the true \\(k\\)-token state, and compares the native prediction with the exact counterfactual oracle. At \\(L=k+1\\), changing position 0 provides a matched **irrelevant-token control** because that position lies outside the true Markov state.\n",
    "\n",
    "A second, mechanistically stronger stage runs **layer-wise activation patching** at \\(L=k+1\\): after each encoder layer, the final-position residual stream from a counterfactual run is patched into the factual run, then the remaining layers and native head are evaluated. The same patch is repeated using an irrelevant-token counterfactual as a control.\n",
    "\n",
    "The primary input-intervention metric is the reduction in KL divergence to the target oracle:\n",
    "\\[\n",
    "G = D_{\\mathrm{KL}}(P_{\\mathrm{target}}\\Vert Q_{\\mathrm{before}})\n",
    "  - D_{\\mathrm{KL}}(P_{\\mathrm{target}}\\Vert Q_{\\mathrm{after}}).\n",
    "\\]\n",
    "\n",
    "For activation patching, the analogous gain compares the factual native prediction with the prediction obtained after patching a counterfactual internal activation.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Claim guardrail\n",
    "The input intervention establishes functional dependence of the scratch model's native prediction on state-defining input. The activation-patching stage provides stronger causal evidence that internal residual-stream information induced by the state change can steer the native prediction. Neither analysis establishes causal use of Qwen/Pythia probe representations, a unique internal state code, or a uniquely identified mechanistic circuit.\n",
    "\n",
    "All outputs are written to a new `Part1/causal_intervention/` directory. Existing checkpoints are read-only.\n"
   ]
  },
